# Drives GitHub's "Cite this repository" button, and is read by Zenodo when
# it mints a DOI for a release.
#
# Two distinct works are involved and should not be conflated. This file
# describes the *catalog* — the data and the site. The seed paper it derives
# from is a separate publication by other authors, recorded under
# `references` so that anyone citing the catalog is pointed at it too.
#
# Once Zenodo has minted the concept DOI, add it under `identifiers` below
# and set the same value in `ZENODO_DOI` in `src/config/site.ts`, which is
# what the site's own citation blocks read.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "projectcert: an atlas of English Learner teacher certification across the 51 state education agencies"
message: "If you use this catalog, please cite both it and the seed paper listed under references."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A catalog of how each U.S. state and the District of Columbia licenses
  teachers to instruct classified English Learner students: bilingual
  education and English Language Development credentials, Sheltered English
  Instruction mandates, Seal of Biliteracy adoption, English language
  proficiency assessments, and the classified English Learner share of public
  school enrollment. Every fact-bearing field traces to a dated, retrievable
  source document.
authors:
  - name: projectcert
repository-code: "https://github.com/jleider/projectcert"
url: "https://projectcert.org"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - English Learner
  - teacher certification
  - bilingual education
  - education policy
  - state education agency
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Decentralization, teacher quality, and the education of English learners: Do state education agencies effectively prepare teachers of ELs?"
    # Initials, matching how the paper is cited throughout this repository
    # and in CitationBlock.astro. Do not expand these to full given names
    # without checking the paper itself — LAUNCH-TODO.md carries a set of
    # expansions that do not reconcile with these initials, so at least one
    # of the two is wrong.
    authors:
      - family-names: Leider
        given-names: C. M.
      - family-names: Colombo
        given-names: M. W.
      - family-names: Nerlino
        given-names: E.
    journal: Education Policy Analysis Archives
    volume: 29
    issue: 100
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.14507/epaa.29.5279
